.TH XNAMESPACE 1 "2026-07-01" "go-x11proto" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xnamespace \- manage server-side X\-NAMESPACE namespaces and their auth tokens
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xnamespace
.RB [ \-s | \-\-short | \-json ]
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xnamespace
is a command\-line client for the X\-NAMESPACE X server extension. It lists,
creates, queries and deletes server\-side namespaces and manages their
authentication tokens.
.PP
The extension is privileged: against a server that does not offer it, or from an
unprivileged client, the commands fail with
.RB \(lq "extension not available" \(rq.
.SH OPTIONS
By default output is human\-readable. For programmatic callers two machine
formats are available; errors always go to standard error, so check the exit
status.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-short
Terse, TAB\-separated, header\-less output: values only, one record per line.
Trivially parsed from a shell
.RB ( $(...) ", " read ", " cut )
or C
.RB ( strtok / fscanf ).
An empty result prints nothing. Takes precedence over
.BR \-json .
.TP
.B \-json
Structured JSON, for richer consumers.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B version
Show the extension version.
.TP
.B list
List all namespaces.
.TP
.BI "create " "name " [ cap ...]\ [transient]
Create a namespace with the given capabilities.
.TP
.BI "delete " "name " [kill]
Delete a namespace;
.B kill
also terminates its clients.
.TP
.BI "query " name
Show one namespace.
.TP
.BI "setflags " "name " <+cap|\-cap>...
Change capability bits.
.TP
.BI "whoami " [resource\-id]
Show the calling client's (or a resource's) namespace.
.TP
.BI "addtoken " "name proto hexdata"
Add an authentication token; prints the new token handle.
.TP
.BI "rmtoken " "name handle"
Remove an authentication token.
.TP
.BI "tokens " name
List a namespace's authentication tokens. No key material is ever shown.
.SH "SHORT OUTPUT FORMAT"
With
.BR \-s ,
each command emits TAB\-separated fields, no header, one record per line:
.PP
.nf
.RS
version    MAJOR.MINOR
list       name  caps(csv)  attrs(csv)  clients  tokens
create     name
delete     name
query      one "key<TAB>value" line per field
setflags   caps(csv)
whoami     name  client|server
addtoken   0xHANDLE
rmtoken    name
tokens     0xHANDLE  proto
.RE
.fi
.SH CAPABILITIES
.B mouse shape transparency input keyboard admin all
.SH EXAMPLES
Create a namespace with two capabilities:
.PP
.RS
.B xnamespace create sandbox mouse keyboard
.RE
.PP
Add a token and capture its handle in a script:
.PP
.RS
.B h=$(xnamespace \-s addtoken sandbox MIT\-MAGIC\-COOKIE\-1 00112233445566778899aabbccddeeff)
.RE
.PP
Report the caller's namespace (prints e.g.
.RB \(lq "sandbox\etclient" \(rq):
.PP
.RS
.B xnamespace \-s whoami
.RE
.PP
List namespaces, one per line, for a shell loop:
.PP
.RS
.B xnamespace \-s list | while IFS="$(printf '\et')" read \-r name caps attrs clients tokens; do ...; done
.RE
.PP
Tear it down, terminating any clients:
.PP
.RS
.B xnamespace delete sandbox kill
.RE
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An error (e.g. the extension is unavailable, or a request was rejected).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (unknown or incomplete command).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR Xserver (1)
